<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Providence</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Providence is the most populous island of the Bahamas, home of the capital Nassau. Settled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleuthera">Eleuthera</a> in the 17th century, it was repeatedly raided by the Spanish and French, and in the early 18th century became the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a>' republic. Today it is the centre of the country's tourism and banking.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-providence.jpg" alt="New Providence" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Providence_in_Bahamas.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
